course: dictionary
lesson: 1167
title: Brittle: hard but easy to break
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Brittle describes something that is hard but breaks easily. A brittle thing snaps or cracks instead of bending.
explain: «Dead branches are dry and brittle and can snap without warning.» The word snap is the clue. Brittle things break suddenly, while flexible things bend.
explain: Brittle can also describe a sound or mood. A brittle voice or laugh sounds sharp and tense, as if it might break. Check the other words around it to decide which meaning fits.
fact: Brittle means hard but easily broken, snapping or cracking instead of bending.
fact: Glass, china and dry twigs are brittle. Rubber is flexible, and metals are often tough.
fact: «Brittle bones» and «brittle hair» break easily. Calcium helps keep bones from getting brittle.
fact: A brittle voice, laugh or mood sounds sharp and tense, as if it might break.
fact: Peanut brittle is a hard sweet made of melted sugar with nuts in it.
exercise: «Dead branches are dry and brittle and can snap without warning.» What does brittle mean here? | Wet and heavy | Soft and bendy | *Hard but easily broken, snapping instead of bending
exercise: «Her laugh was brittle, sharp and tense, as if it might crack.» What does brittle suggest about her laugh? | *Sharp and tense, as if it might break | Warm and cosy | Loud and happy
exercise: Mia says peanut brittle is a kind of bread. What is peanut brittle? | A soft cheese | A kind of bread | *A hard sweet made of melted sugar with nuts in it | A cold drink
test: Which material is brittle? | *Glass | Metal spoon that bends | Rubber band
test: «Calcium helps keep bones from getting brittle.» What would happen to bones that are brittle? | *They could snap or crack more easily | They bend easily without breaking | They grow longer | They become flexible like rubber
exam: In «Run through the long grass in shorts and the nettles bite back: their hairs are tiny brittle needles that snap and push stinging chemicals into your skin», which words are the clues to the meaning of brittle? | Long grass and shorts | Bite back and sting | *Snap and push, because brittle needles break and do not bend | Run through and nettles
